  "handoffOracle": "005/PT-BAT-030..037: parent single session lock -> child dedicated-role transaction lock -> parent nonblocking reacquire; repeated handoff preserves exact one acquisition. Missing/shared/two-int/reentrant/state/interrupt/null reject, every observed JDBC occurrence and each of5 scalar missing/duplicate/null/flipped/null-resource faults reject, resources close and provider diagnostics stay absent. Child IOException fixed, unexpected Runtime/Error identity preserved, null result never succeeds. A competing real connection/thread in the gap prevents parent success without waiting/force unlock.",
  "recordOracle": "007/PT-BAT-038..045: hand-written ASCII anchor72/activation109/done140 or141 bytes; nil/max UUID, UTC0001/9999 and microseconds, Asia/Tokyo civil date boundaries,0/10 only. Each fixed magic/delimiter byte mutated to all other byte values; aliases, leap normalization, scalar errors, malformed/null and wrong model reject. Valid different identity remains different data, not authentication. Completion invariants, caller-owned arrays, redacted values and64 independent activations use literal field/byte oracles.",
  "durableRecordOracle": "009/PT-BAT-046..057: independent literal records and real private inode/no-replace/fsync with synthetic root admission. Borrowed-root canonical name-to-content binding; bounded read, same-content reuse only, expected-inode retirement, every independently counted native/IO occurrence fails closed and releases owned resources; namespace replacement, metadata/ACL/filesystem, null, invalid IO, interruption and concurrency. No partial-file overwrite or automatic cleanup.",
  "lifecycleOracle": "011/PT-BAT-058..081: fixed six-root namespace and scope-bound session, complete unfiltered canonical inventory, original-inode snapshots through whole-graph scan, anchor/begin/done/active consistency and unique pending run. Literal start/resume/complete and crash states, no new cutoff on resume, immutable prior completion, same-byte recovery force/directory sync and absent retirement re-sync, independently counted native/IO fault locations, null/closed/interrupt/runtime and concurrency. Root admission is synthetic over actual local inodes; parent OS lock and legacy DB uniqueness are caller obligations.",
